---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="Privacy policy and data collection details for StackVerdict."
	pubDate={new Date('October 01 2026')}
>
	<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
	<p><em>Last updated: October 2026</em></p>

	<p>
		At <strong>StackVerdict</strong> (accessible from stackverdict.netlify.app), protecting reader privacy is one of our main priorities. This Privacy Policy outlines the types of information collected and recorded by our site.
	</p>

	<h2>Information We Collect</h2>
	<p>
		StackVerdict is built as a static JAMstack site hosted on Netlify. We do not collect personal identification information (PII) like names, phone numbers, or passwords unless you voluntarily submit them via a contact or newsletter subscription form.
	</p>

	<h2>Log Files & Analytics</h2>
	<p>
		Like most websites, StackVerdict utilizes standard server log files and lightweight web analytics (e.g., Netlify Analytics / Google Analytics) to analyze trends, administer the site, and track user navigation on the site. This data includes IP addresses, browser types, ISP provider details, and page visitation metrics, none of which are linked to personally identifiable information.
	</p>

	<h2>Cookies & Web Beacons</h2>
	<p>
		StackVerdict may use basic cookies to store user preferences and optimize site responsiveness. Third-party affiliate partners (such as PartnerStack or Impact) may use cookies on their end to track referral traffic when you click on an outbound software link.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact Us</h2>
	<p>
		If you have additional questions or require more information about our Privacy Policy, feel free to reach out to us at <code>contact@stackverdict.com</code>.
	</p>
</Layout>